PARTS.md: parts on Waterfall, stacks attested here, outside testers who only release a result

A proposal doc, no code. It turns TECHNIQUES.md into a shape and logs one rule as settled.

## The rule it records
- Every upload carries a needs list of human/hardware tests.
- Anyone can take the bedshock-rigged build; results fold back in.
- The tester's only act is releasing the result: no accounts, keys, tokens, passwords, codes or forms. Flows that need one are not candidates.
- Minimum: a completion manifest, verified on return, and public stats.
- Transport deliberately unsolved; the space stays open rather than filled with a compromised flow.

## The shape
- part / library / stack / board. Waterfall keeps the files, bedshock vouches for them.
- `features` (written) vs `spec` (computed from the bundle, incl. API members checked against the declared module, which is what would have caught Zero Fall 1.0.0).
- Board: append-only attestations, STANDING / SUSPECT / BROKEN per stack per version, collision and double-load checks.
- A one-page brief for an agent building and lodging a part.
- Build order: check follows imports, spec extractor, part kind on Waterfall, board, rigged build.

## Merge qualifications
- [x] docs only; README "Where things are" row and a pointer from TECHNIQUES.md
- [ ] owner reads the rule section and confirms it says what was meant

